  "slug": "environment-shape-regulatory-variation-1c31",
  "summary": "Five preprints show that reference choice and haplotype-resolved genomes alter the genetic interpretation of plant traits and RNA-seq measurements.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that genotype-linked interpretation depends on the reference framework. A parent-of-origin-resolved Granny Smith apple genome shows that matched references expose sun-exposure and cold-storage responses that other references miss. In Capsicum, a 48-genome super-pangenome resolves structural variation and NLR resistance gene diversity, while a pangenome-guided k-mer GWAS links pungency and aroma terpene traits to Pun1 haplotypes and TPS genes. Mapping strategy is a related variable: a comparison of genome-guided and transcriptome-guided RNA-seq quantification across six plant species reports quantification bias for tandemly duplicated genes. The Tipularia discolor study, based on a fragmented assembly, mines candidate genes for sucrose, terpenoid and phenylpropanoid metabolism. What is new is the use of haplotype-resolved and pangenome frameworks to resolve allele-specific and reference-dependent variation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
